1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,294
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,378 --> 00:00:08,591
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,675 --> 00:00:10,802
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:12,762
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:16,391
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,474 --> 00:00:17,350
[Red, in English] Kill me now.

7
00:00:17,434 --> 00:00:18,435
[in English] Kill me now!

8
00:00:18,518 --> 00:00:20,353
[Dmitri, in English] <i>You're not worth it.</i>

9
00:00:20,437 --> 00:00:21,438
- [gunshots]
- [groans]

10
00:00:21,521 --> 00:00:23,064
[gunshots]

11
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:24,232
- [gunshots]
- [Janine, indistinct]

12
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:25,275
[sobbing]

13
00:00:25,358 --> 00:00:26,526
[in English] Dad!

14
00:00:26,609 --> 00:00:28,153
- Audrey, run away!
- [in English] No!

15
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:31,114
[in English] I'm not leaving you
and my daughter, Dad! No!

16
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:32,032
[sobs]

17
00:00:32,115 --> 00:00:33,366
She's not really your daughter.

18
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:34,659
[gasps]

19
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:37,287
[in English] Resting for focus,
focus! I'm right here!

20
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:38,371
[grunts]

21
00:00:38,455 --> 00:00:39,581
[grunting and groaning]

22
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:40,707
PREVIOUSLY

23
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:42,125
‪[clanging and clattering]

24
00:00:42,208 --> 00:00:45,962
Is it okay if you go to my school?

25
00:00:46,671 --> 00:00:49,841
- Because Tatoy might not be there yet.
- [buzzing]

26
00:00:49,924 --> 00:00:51,968
[Olga] <i>Um, why… Why is that?</i>

27
00:00:52,051 --> 00:00:54,512
Our moving-up ceremony is near.

28
00:00:54,596 --> 00:00:56,431
Where is my real child?!

29
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:59,517
I'll never tell you, even if you shoot me.

30
00:00:59,601 --> 00:01:01,394
[gasping]

31
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:02,395
- [grunts]
- [screams]

32
00:01:02,479 --> 00:01:03,521
Stop it, Red!

33
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:04,856
- [gunshots]
- [grunts]

34
00:01:04,939 --> 00:01:07,650
- [groans and screams]
- [in English] Dad!

35
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:09,110
[echoing]

36
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:11,488
[Atoy] We won't be able
to get out anymore.

37
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:12,906
We'll rot here.

38
00:01:12,989 --> 00:01:15,909
Just think of the people who love you.

39
00:01:15,992 --> 00:01:18,119
No one cares about me now.

40
00:01:18,203 --> 00:01:20,288
[Atoy] <i>My life has no meaning anymore.</i>

41
00:01:20,371 --> 00:01:21,790
[in English] Mission status.

42
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:24,292
[in English] Outside the establishment.

43
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:27,962
[in English] Potential headquarters
of Anthony "Atoy" Padua.

44
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:30,715
[Lily] <i>Even if you say</i>
<i>you don't have a family,</i>

45
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:34,385
<i>surely, you left a mark</i>
<i>on at least one person.</i>

46
00:01:34,469 --> 00:01:35,845
[huffing]

47
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:44,562
[music fades]

48
00:01:47,273 --> 00:01:49,984
[suspicious music playing]

49
00:02:02,372 --> 00:02:09,045
[indistinct chattering]

50
00:02:09,129 --> 00:02:10,880
- Hey, guys!
- [exclaims]

51
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:14,300
Papa Uno, my night is complete
because I saw you. You're so handsome!

52
00:02:14,384 --> 00:02:15,718
- [chuckles]
- [group giggles]

53
00:02:15,802 --> 00:02:17,887
Hi, Papa Uno. I mean, Uno.

54
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:21,182
Maybe you'd like to join us,
only if you can.

55
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:23,393
Because Brother Kurt has free pares.

56
00:02:23,476 --> 00:02:24,310
- Yes.
- If you can, Papa Uno.

57
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:26,396
[Denden] Oh, no, T-Bak looks possessed.

58
00:02:26,479 --> 00:02:27,981
Are you okay?

59
00:02:28,064 --> 00:02:29,649
He's just hungry!

60
00:02:29,732 --> 00:02:32,235
Papa Uno, what do you say?

61
00:02:32,318 --> 00:02:33,153
Come with us.

62
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:36,030
- Hmm, okay. Okay, let's go.
- [Jona] Oh, no!

63
00:02:36,114 --> 00:02:38,074
- You agreed?
- Yes!

64
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:39,117
- Let's go.
- Yes!

65
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,326
- There! He agreed.
- [Karla] Wait a minute.

66
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:42,579
Maybe we're bothering Uno.

67
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:43,538
- No, not at all!
- [T-Bak] Hey.

68
00:02:43,621 --> 00:02:44,706
[indistinct chattering]

69
00:02:44,789 --> 00:02:46,332
Bothering me? No way!

70
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:49,752
Actually, I'm really hungry too.

71
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:51,921
- Oh, there you go!
- Let's go! I'll join you.

72
00:02:52,005 --> 00:02:53,089
- Where is it? Let's go.
- [lively chatter]

73
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:54,883
So, what are you doing here at the shop?

74
00:02:55,466 --> 00:02:57,385
- Here? Uh…
- [Karla] Yes.

75
00:02:57,969 --> 00:02:59,679
I came to have a suit made.

76
00:02:59,762 --> 00:03:04,100
They told me
this is really the best place.

77
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:05,226
- You know?
- [muttering]

78
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:06,853
- Great tailoring, so…
- [overlapping chatter]

79
00:03:06,936 --> 00:03:08,104
So I came here.

80
00:03:08,187 --> 00:03:09,188
Yes, that's it.

81
00:03:09,272 --> 00:03:11,107
But too bad, Brother Atoy isn't here.

82
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:12,692
No one can take your measurements.

83
00:03:13,526 --> 00:03:14,986
Exactly.

84
00:03:15,069 --> 00:03:16,779
I noticed that too.

85
00:03:17,447 --> 00:03:19,407
I noticed he's not there.

86
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:21,826
But anyway.

87
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:24,037
Maybe I'll just borrow instead.

88
00:03:24,662 --> 00:03:26,456
Hmm. What's that?

89
00:03:26,539 --> 00:03:27,624
What did you put in your pocket?

90
00:03:28,666 --> 00:03:29,918
- Huh? Hey.
- Are you hiding something?

91
00:03:30,001 --> 00:03:32,795
- What are you hiding? Show us!
- [overlapping chatter]

92
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:33,838
They say you're hiding something.

93
00:03:33,922 --> 00:03:35,089
[Jona] What's that? Show us.

94
00:03:35,173 --> 00:03:36,174
[Mona] Let us see.

95
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:37,133
Show us what you're hiding.

96
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:39,761
- There is. There really is.
- Ahh!

97
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:42,430
- [Jona] Hey.
- Wait. Yes. There is, there is.

98
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:44,807
- Oh no! Surprise!
- What's that? What's that?

99
00:03:44,891 --> 00:03:47,936
No, honestly, this is really for Karla.

100
00:03:48,019 --> 00:03:49,604
- Wow!
- I really want to give this to you.

101
00:03:49,687 --> 00:03:51,731
- [Jona] For Karla? Oh, what--
- Karla, this is for you.

102
00:03:51,814 --> 00:03:54,025
- [exclaiming]
- [sneaky music playing]

103
00:03:54,108 --> 00:03:56,819
Oh my! You're lucky you're cute!

104
00:03:56,903 --> 00:03:58,279
I can tolerate you. Me, as if?!

105
00:03:58,363 --> 00:03:59,322
[muttering]

106
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:00,907
Oh my. I can't stand my hunger anymore!

107
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:02,992
- Let's go!
- Exactly!

108
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:04,535
- Let's go!
- [lively chattering]

109
00:04:04,619 --> 00:04:06,955
Let's go, Papa. Papa Uno.

110
00:04:08,539 --> 00:04:10,875
[indistinct chattering]

111
00:04:16,256 --> 00:04:17,966
- [music fades]
- [door clicks open]

112
00:04:18,841 --> 00:04:20,468
[sinister music playing]

113
00:04:20,551 --> 00:04:21,511
Boss.

114
00:04:22,428 --> 00:04:24,222
Audrey and Janine have already left.

115
00:04:25,098 --> 00:04:26,224
How?

116
00:04:26,724 --> 00:04:28,768
Your son brought them.

117
00:04:28,851 --> 00:04:32,689
[music intensifies]

118
00:04:34,315 --> 00:04:37,068
[line rings]

119
00:04:38,027 --> 00:04:41,531
Gav, are you with Audrey? Go home now.

120
00:04:41,614 --> 00:04:44,784
[Gavin on the phone] <i>No, Dad.</i>
<i>Tell me the truth first.</i>

121
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:46,119
[Gavin sobs]

122
00:04:46,202 --> 00:04:47,829
[in English] <i>Did you kill Grandpa?</i>

123
00:04:47,912 --> 00:04:49,455
We'll talk about it when you get home.

124
00:04:49,539 --> 00:04:51,249
[Gavin on the phone] <i>Answer me first, Dad!</i>

125
00:04:51,332 --> 00:04:54,002
Whatever your aunt told you,
it's more complicated than that.

126
00:04:54,085 --> 00:04:55,420
[Gavin on the phone] <i>So, it's true!</i>

127
00:04:55,503 --> 00:04:57,547
<i>How could you do that?!</i>

128
00:04:57,630 --> 00:04:59,966
<i>Your niece, your sister, and then…</i>

129
00:05:00,049 --> 00:05:02,593
<i>Even your own father.</i>
<i>You hurt all of them?</i>

130
00:05:03,386 --> 00:05:05,388
<i>What's next? Me?</i>

131
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:07,682
[in English] <i>Are you going</i>
<i>to kill me too, Dad?</i>

132
00:05:07,765 --> 00:05:09,851
[music fades]

133
00:05:12,228 --> 00:05:15,273
[suave theme music playing]

134
00:05:15,982 --> 00:05:18,067
[motorcycle revving]

135
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:19,652
[sewing machine whirring]

136
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:20,611
[scratches]

137
00:05:20,695 --> 00:05:21,571
[snipping]

138
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:24,115
[sewing machine clacking]

139
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:27,285
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

140
00:05:27,368 --> 00:05:29,871
[gunshots]

141
00:05:29,954 --> 00:05:31,622
[clicking]

142
00:05:31,706 --> 00:05:33,583
[snipping]

143
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:37,420
[music swells]

144
00:05:37,503 --> 00:05:39,422
[electronic blipping]

145
00:05:40,965 --> 00:05:43,217
[music fades]

146
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:52,727
[suspicious music playing]

147
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:53,728
Madam.

148
00:05:55,855 --> 00:05:56,689
[in English] Where's the girl?

149
00:05:58,024 --> 00:05:59,358
Can I sit first?

150
00:06:03,821 --> 00:06:04,781
Uh, oh.

151
00:06:05,656 --> 00:06:08,576
I heard the coffee here is good.

152
00:06:09,327 --> 00:06:11,412
Would you like some, madam? My treat.

153
00:06:11,496 --> 00:06:12,914
[in English] What are you trying to do?

154
00:06:15,958 --> 00:06:18,294
Our deal was that today,
you'll give us back the kid.

155
00:06:18,377 --> 00:06:21,422
Because, madam, she's at home.

156
00:06:21,506 --> 00:06:23,925
But she's with Charmi.

157
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:25,676
Um…

158
00:06:26,552 --> 00:06:30,681
Honestly, I don't want you
to worry anymore.

159
00:06:30,765 --> 00:06:32,850
And I don't want you
to have problems with the kid,

160
00:06:32,934 --> 00:06:35,186
so, it's okay
if I take care of her instead.

161
00:06:36,229 --> 00:06:37,522
What are you saying?

162
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:41,359
Uh, maybe…

163
00:06:41,859 --> 00:06:44,278
Maybe, madam, I could…

164
00:06:46,072 --> 00:06:48,366
take care of the child.

165
00:06:48,449 --> 00:06:51,953
Uh, adopt her, like that. [titters]

166
00:06:52,036 --> 00:06:52,954
Can I?

167
00:06:53,538 --> 00:06:54,705
[in English] Of course not.

168
00:06:55,289 --> 00:06:57,333
You need to give her back to me.

169
00:06:58,292 --> 00:07:01,796
But how, madam? Because…

170
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:05,216
The child already believes I'm her mother.

171
00:07:05,299 --> 00:07:07,260
Can't we just make it real?

172
00:07:07,343 --> 00:07:09,178
You won't have to worry anymore.

173
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:11,389
No payment, free of charge.

174
00:07:11,472 --> 00:07:12,723
No.

175
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:14,725
- And don't ask why. Just return the--
- [phone ringing]

176
00:07:19,063 --> 00:07:20,440
[in English] Can you
just stay here, please?

177
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:22,108
[in English] I-I need to take this call.

178
00:07:22,191 --> 00:07:23,401
[phone blips]

179
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:25,445
What?

180
00:07:26,112 --> 00:07:27,905
She's about to tell her husband.

181
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:30,700
It's chaos here. Come home.

182
00:07:31,284 --> 00:07:32,743
They might do something to me.

183
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:35,288
I can't yet. The child isn't here.

184
00:07:35,371 --> 00:07:36,456
Olga didn't bring her.

185
00:07:37,248 --> 00:07:38,416
Why?

186
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,377
[in English] I don't know.
She wants the kid to herself.

187
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:44,255
We need the child.

188
00:07:45,631 --> 00:07:47,133
Audrey escaped,

189
00:07:47,216 --> 00:07:49,802
and the child is the only way
to bring Audrey back here,

190
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:51,179
so she won't speak.

191
00:07:51,762 --> 00:07:54,515
What the hell, hon? How did Audrey escape?

192
00:07:54,599 --> 00:07:57,685
That's not important.
I just-- I just need the kid, okay?

193
00:07:58,227 --> 00:08:00,521
[in English] Fine. I'll see what I can do.

194
00:08:01,105 --> 00:08:02,273
Hurry!

195
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:05,026
Audrey might do something.

196
00:08:05,109 --> 00:08:07,069
[suspicious music playing]

197
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:09,113
She already knows Janine isn't her child.

198
00:08:09,697 --> 00:08:11,324
Just think what Atoy will do

199
00:08:11,407 --> 00:08:14,285
when he finds out
Ibyang is really his true child.

200
00:08:14,368 --> 00:08:15,786
[music fades]

201
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:17,830
Ibyang is Atoy's child?

202
00:08:18,748 --> 00:08:19,624
What did you hear?

203
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:21,667
Nothing, madam.

204
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:24,378
Uh--

205
00:08:25,213 --> 00:08:26,589
[in English] Stop right there, Olga.

206
00:08:26,672 --> 00:08:28,382
Why are you in such a hurry to leave?

207
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:30,092
We're not done talking.

208
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:33,221
Uh, you said it, didn't you?

209
00:08:34,263 --> 00:08:37,850
That Atoy is Ibyang's real father?

210
00:08:38,684 --> 00:08:39,977
Then why…

211
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:42,480
Why don't you tell him the truth?

212
00:08:42,563 --> 00:08:43,773
Why are you hiding it?

213
00:08:44,357 --> 00:08:47,401
[in English] That's none of your business,
and you better keep your mouth shut.

214
00:08:47,485 --> 00:08:48,611
We paid you.

215
00:08:49,195 --> 00:08:52,365
Yes. You paid me to pretend
to be Ibyang's mother.

216
00:08:52,448 --> 00:08:54,992
But not to lie to Atoy.

217
00:08:55,076 --> 00:08:57,286
[in English] What do you want?
More money? How much?

218
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:58,704
Just to shut your mouth.

219
00:08:58,788 --> 00:08:59,956
- Oh, so--
- Money is all you care about.

220
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:02,542
Look at you. You talk so big.

221
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:06,671
Sure, you're rich, you have money,
but your fart stinks too!

222
00:09:06,754 --> 00:09:07,964
We're just the same!

223
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:09,882
So, if you belittle me,

224
00:09:10,466 --> 00:09:13,886
I'd rather tell Atoy everything.

225
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:16,389
- [in English] Not so fast!
- Ouch!

226
00:09:16,889 --> 00:09:19,350
- [grunting]
- [groaning]

227
00:09:19,433 --> 00:09:22,395
You're really messing with my hair, huh!

228
00:09:22,478 --> 00:09:24,564
Hey, don't underestimate me!

229
00:09:24,647 --> 00:09:25,982
I'm a fighter too!

230
00:09:26,941 --> 00:09:28,901
You think you're decent people.

231
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:30,903
Wow, turns out your evil
is on a whole different level.

232
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:32,905
Good thing I didn't bring Ibyang here!

233
00:09:32,989 --> 00:09:33,948
[Olga scoffs]

234
00:09:34,031 --> 00:09:35,116
Good luck to you,

235
00:09:35,199 --> 00:09:37,034
because I'll tell Atoy everything,

236
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:38,160
and Atoy will deal with you!

237
00:09:38,244 --> 00:09:39,245
You're not going to do that,

238
00:09:39,328 --> 00:09:40,913
because you're going to surrender
Ibyang to me!

239
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:42,206
[in English] Make me!

240
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:43,124
[smirks]

241
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:44,542
Just a warning, okay.

242
00:09:46,210 --> 00:09:48,462
I'm not only a good actress,

243
00:09:49,547 --> 00:09:51,424
I'm also good at martial arts.

244
00:09:52,258 --> 00:09:54,176
Brown belter here!

245
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:56,220
[tense music playing]

246
00:09:57,513 --> 00:09:58,347
Ouch! [groans]

247
00:09:58,431 --> 00:10:00,099
So, you think you can scare me?!

248
00:10:00,182 --> 00:10:01,267
- Huh?!
- Ouch!

249
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:03,519
Your bag may be expensive,

250
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:05,271
but mine is tougher!

251
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:06,731
[grunting and groaning]

252
00:10:06,814 --> 00:10:08,190
[pained grunting]

253
00:10:08,983 --> 00:10:10,818
[in English] What the hell
is inside your bag?!

254
00:10:10,901 --> 00:10:12,528
What?! It hurts, doesn't it?

255
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:15,448
That's what happens
when your bag is full of coins!

256
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:20,161
[shrieks, coughing]

257
00:10:22,663 --> 00:10:23,956
[in English] Somebody help me!

258
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:24,874
- [coughs]
- Ma'am, ma'am!

259
00:10:24,957 --> 00:10:26,667
- What happened to you, ma'am?
- [coughs]

260
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:28,878
[in English] You idiots!
You let her get away!

261
00:10:28,961 --> 00:10:30,087
[security guard] Chase her, chase her!

262
00:10:30,171 --> 00:10:32,673
- [coughs]
- [music fades]

263
00:10:34,091 --> 00:10:35,635
Here, dude. I'm telling you.

264
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:37,803
[in English] Best pares
in all of Tabang Lupa!

265
00:10:37,887 --> 00:10:40,514
- It's solid. Mmm-hmm.
- [Kurt] Try it.

266
00:10:41,265 --> 00:10:42,642
It's really solid!

267
00:10:42,725 --> 00:10:44,143
It's delicious. It's true!

268
00:10:44,226 --> 00:10:45,686
Mmm. Really delicious.

269
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:48,439
- [Bunda] Oh.
- Especially the soup, Brother Kurt.

270
00:10:48,522 --> 00:10:49,940
Mmm, so good.

271
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:52,610
- You're good at eating soup.
- Mmm.

272
00:10:52,693 --> 00:10:55,029
I think it'll taste better if I add this--

273
00:10:55,112 --> 00:10:57,156
Ah, wait! Wait.

274
00:10:57,239 --> 00:10:58,991
- I'll handle that.
- No, I'll do it.

275
00:10:59,075 --> 00:11:00,910
No, hey! I'll handle it.

276
00:11:00,993 --> 00:11:02,536
I can do this.

277
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:04,163
- Really? Okay then.
- Yes, it spilled.

278
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:07,166
[Bunda] There. We've got garlic.

279
00:11:07,249 --> 00:11:10,086
- There, it's delicious.
- And this one.

280
00:11:10,169 --> 00:11:12,963
I don't know what it's called. [chuckles]

281
00:11:13,714 --> 00:11:16,133
- [in English] Oh, thank you.
- There.

282
00:11:16,217 --> 00:11:18,302
There. Okay, let's try it.

283
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:19,720
[in English] Enjoy.

284
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:20,805
Mmm-hmm.

285
00:11:20,888 --> 00:11:22,681
Oh, right? Oh!

286
00:11:22,765 --> 00:11:24,892
- I feel something.
- What?

287
00:11:24,975 --> 00:11:27,061
- You're thirsty.
- [chuckles]

288
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:28,521
You're good! Mmm-hmm.

289
00:11:28,604 --> 00:11:29,730
I'm good, right?

290
00:11:29,814 --> 00:11:32,400
That's why I also have water for you.

291
00:11:32,483 --> 00:11:34,068
- Wow!
- [Bunda] Mmm-hmm.

292
00:11:34,151 --> 00:11:35,319
- Hey, Bunda!
- Why?

293
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:36,987
- [in English] Thank you.
- Hey, show some respect.

294
00:11:37,071 --> 00:11:38,656
The person's eating.

295
00:11:38,739 --> 00:11:40,199
He can't eat properly anymore.

296
00:11:40,282 --> 00:11:42,952
Miss Siony, this is my moment!

297
00:11:43,035 --> 00:11:44,703
[Uno] It's okay, Miss Siony.

298
00:11:44,787 --> 00:11:45,621
I'm really okay.

299
00:11:45,704 --> 00:11:46,997
Ah, because, well--

300
00:11:47,081 --> 00:11:48,666
[Uno] Eat now. It's okay. It's okay.

301
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:51,210
Hey, Karla.

302
00:11:51,961 --> 00:11:53,546
Your stare is quite different.

303
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:56,757
It's clinging, like body odor!

304
00:11:57,466 --> 00:11:58,467
Crazy!

305
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:02,263
I saw Uno opening Brother Atoy's gate.

306
00:12:02,346 --> 00:12:04,640
Then he suddenly hid his tool.

307
00:12:05,224 --> 00:12:07,101
[T-Bak] Really? No way?

308
00:12:08,102 --> 00:12:10,521
Yes. Hello?

309
00:12:10,604 --> 00:12:12,815
We don't even know him.

310
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:15,151
He just suddenly appeared here.

311
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:17,945
[Karla] Maybe he's Brother Atoy's enemy.

312
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:20,656
That's why he's here, to take revenge.

313
00:12:20,739 --> 00:12:25,411
- [suspicious music playing]
- [indistinct chattering]

314
00:12:25,494 --> 00:12:26,829
Doesn't seem like it!

315
00:12:27,329 --> 00:12:29,623
You know what? You're just AS!

316
00:12:29,707 --> 00:12:30,833
Always suspicious!

317
00:12:31,834 --> 00:12:33,043
- [scoffs]
- [Indistinct chattering]

318
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:34,587
- It's delicious, right?
- Mmm-hmm.

319
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:35,504
[Bunda] More water?

320
00:12:35,588 --> 00:12:36,714
Well, you're the one paying. Right?

321
00:12:36,797 --> 00:12:38,883
[Bunda] What did you say?

322
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:40,509
- I need banana cue.
- [indistinct chattering]

323
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:45,222
- Huh?
- [suspicious music playing]

324
00:12:46,849 --> 00:12:47,892
[T-Bak] What are you planning?

325
00:12:47,975 --> 00:12:50,227
[indistinct chattering]

326
00:12:51,687 --> 00:12:52,980
Discount?

327
00:12:53,063 --> 00:12:55,858
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

328
00:12:56,650 --> 00:12:58,402
[chuckles] Do you want more?

329
00:12:58,486 --> 00:13:00,821
The egg is delicious, isn't it?

330
00:13:00,905 --> 00:13:01,947
[chuckles]

331
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:03,616
[music fades]

332
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:07,661
[Charmi] Don't move!

333
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:09,747
[rousing music playing]

334
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:12,791
[gentle music playing]

335
00:13:12,875 --> 00:13:14,084
God…

336
00:13:14,168 --> 00:13:15,377
Charmi!

337
00:13:15,461 --> 00:13:16,420
- [chuckles]
- My God!

338
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:18,339
- [giggles]
- I got nervous--

339
00:13:18,422 --> 00:13:19,548
What's wrong with you?!

340
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:21,300
Why do you have a gun?!

341
00:13:21,383 --> 00:13:23,093
What-- What is that?! It's so big!

342
00:13:23,177 --> 00:13:25,471
Oh, no, it's nothing! It's fake, look!

343
00:13:25,554 --> 00:13:27,264
It's wood, see!

344
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:28,182
[giggles]

345
00:13:28,265 --> 00:13:29,892
You scared me.

346
00:13:29,975 --> 00:13:32,645
It's fake! I asked for it
from the production designer

347
00:13:32,728 --> 00:13:34,605
who's courting me, Egay!

348
00:13:34,688 --> 00:13:35,856
[Charmi] Oh, it's nice, look!

349
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,566
Effective for scaring people.

350
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:38,692
[giggles]

351
00:13:39,443 --> 00:13:40,444
- [Charmi] Oh.
- Hey.

352
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:41,946
[in English] Thank you.

353
00:13:42,446 --> 00:13:44,073
You watched over Ibyang.

354
00:13:45,032 --> 00:13:45,950
Where is she anyway?

355
00:13:46,033 --> 00:13:47,284
Oh, well.

356
00:13:47,368 --> 00:13:49,453
After eating, she went upstairs.

357
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:52,206
I checked the room.
She's been asleep for a while.

358
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:55,793
Hey! What did Madam Martina say?

359
00:13:55,876 --> 00:13:59,004
Did she agree
that you'll be Ibyang's official mother?

360
00:14:03,717 --> 00:14:06,887
- [melancholic music playing]
- Mmm.

361
00:14:10,015 --> 00:14:10,849
Look at this.

362
00:14:10,933 --> 00:14:13,227
We look so cute here.
Like real mother and child, right?

363
00:14:13,310 --> 00:14:15,854
Oh, yes. So cute!

364
00:14:17,481 --> 00:14:20,568
You know, just when I really started
to love that child,

365
00:14:21,193 --> 00:14:24,363
that's when I found out the truth
about her parents.

366
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:25,990
Huh?

367
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:29,827
You know the real--
Ibyang's real parents?!

368
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:31,620
[music fades]

369
00:14:31,704 --> 00:14:32,830
It's Atoy.

370
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:35,082
[sentimental music playing]

371
00:14:35,165 --> 00:14:36,250
[in English] For real?!

372
00:14:36,333 --> 00:14:38,460
It's Atoy? Wait, that's crazy.

373
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:39,545
Wait.

374
00:14:40,462 --> 00:14:43,007
Atoy is Ibyang's real father?!

375
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:47,136
That's why, even though
I want to care for Ibyang

376
00:14:47,219 --> 00:14:50,139
and stand firm that I'll be her mother,

377
00:14:50,222 --> 00:14:52,391
of course, that wouldn't
be right, would it?

378
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:57,187
I still need to give her back
to her real parent.

379
00:14:58,355 --> 00:14:59,273
To Atoy.

380
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:04,111
[music fades]

381
00:15:05,779 --> 00:15:07,489
It's my fault.

382
00:15:08,657 --> 00:15:10,576
Even Emerson got dragged into this.

383
00:15:10,659 --> 00:15:11,493
[sighs]

384
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:14,872
Never mind. Tomorrow,
I'll look for another place to stay.

385
00:15:15,539 --> 00:15:18,083
So Atoy won't get mad at me.
It's embarrassing.

386
00:15:18,667 --> 00:15:20,753
Paldo, come on.

387
00:15:20,836 --> 00:15:22,421
You know Atoy.

388
00:15:22,504 --> 00:15:23,714
If he were here,

389
00:15:23,797 --> 00:15:26,383
he'd be the first
to offer his house to you.

390
00:15:28,719 --> 00:15:29,970
Miss Cita.

391
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:33,474
[clicks tongue] Emerson
once mentioned something to me.

392
00:15:34,808 --> 00:15:36,393
About…

393
00:15:37,811 --> 00:15:39,688
Atoy's other job.

394
00:15:40,814 --> 00:15:43,609
Isn't his mission finished yet?

395
00:15:44,693 --> 00:15:46,195
Maybe.

396
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:50,366
Ame, has Atoy called or texted you?

397
00:15:50,449 --> 00:15:52,201
[pensive music playing]

398
00:15:52,284 --> 00:15:54,244
Just recently.

399
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:58,123
Even if he's very busy,

400
00:15:58,832 --> 00:16:02,169
he always leaves instructions
here at the shop.

401
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:08,801
This is the longest time
he hasn't sent word while on a mission.

402
00:16:08,884 --> 00:16:09,969
Oh.

403
00:16:11,053 --> 00:16:13,681
Paldo, better rest now.

404
00:16:13,764 --> 00:16:16,392
Stay in Atoy's room while he's away.

405
00:16:16,475 --> 00:16:18,602
Emerson is on his way here.

406
00:16:18,686 --> 00:16:21,397
He's just taking care of things
over at his burned shop.

407
00:16:21,981 --> 00:16:24,400
- Ah, okay, Miss Cita.
- [Cita] All right.

408
00:16:25,609 --> 00:16:26,944
Knock, knock.

409
00:16:27,653 --> 00:16:29,613
Uno. Uh…

410
00:16:29,697 --> 00:16:31,115
Good evening.

411
00:16:31,198 --> 00:16:32,408
Do you need something?

412
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:34,410
Uh, sorry.

413
00:16:34,493 --> 00:16:37,413
I came here late.

414
00:16:37,496 --> 00:16:40,332
But I'd like to have a suit made.

415
00:16:40,416 --> 00:16:41,583
I really need it.

416
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:44,670
Oh, sorry. Atoy isn't here.

417
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:48,966
But if you want,
I can take your measurements instead.

418
00:16:49,049 --> 00:16:52,386
- Oh, is that okay?
- Yes, yes.

419
00:16:52,469 --> 00:16:53,345
You write it down.

420
00:16:53,429 --> 00:16:54,263
Okay, okay.

421
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:57,808
Thank you. But is it okay if

422
00:16:57,891 --> 00:16:59,935
I use the restroom?

423
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:02,062
[Uno] If it's okay.

424
00:17:02,146 --> 00:17:03,188
Ah, oh sure, there.

425
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:04,898
Go inside, there.

426
00:17:04,982 --> 00:17:06,066
[Cita] Then straight ahead.

427
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:08,027
- Here?
- [Cita] Yes, yes. That door.

428
00:17:08,110 --> 00:17:09,903
- Straight ahead? Ah, okay. All right.
- [Cita] Yes.

429
00:17:09,987 --> 00:17:12,197
[suspicious music playing]

430
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:13,615
[Paldo] Ah, okay, Miss Cita.

431
00:17:13,699 --> 00:17:16,160
- I'll go upstairs now.
- Ah, okay, okay.

432
00:17:19,496 --> 00:17:22,416
It's better to get
Uno's measurements upstairs.

433
00:17:22,499 --> 00:17:24,084
- Okay.
- Come on.

434
00:17:24,168 --> 00:17:26,962
[Cita sighs]

435
00:17:28,756 --> 00:17:30,549
[music fades]

436
00:17:33,510 --> 00:17:34,636
Ah, Brother Kurt.

437
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,138
[Denden] Oh, Karla.

438
00:17:36,221 --> 00:17:37,890
Any news about Emerson?

439
00:17:37,973 --> 00:17:39,683
Does he still have his things?

440
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:41,351
I don't know.

441
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:42,644
[sneaky music playing]

442
00:17:42,728 --> 00:17:44,063
Wait.

443
00:17:44,646 --> 00:17:45,856
Where are they?

444
00:17:45,939 --> 00:17:47,900
They ate and ran.

445
00:17:47,983 --> 00:17:50,319
Here, I packed your leftovers.

446
00:17:50,402 --> 00:17:51,653
Thanks.

447
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:52,863
Hmm.

448
00:17:52,946 --> 00:17:54,448
[in English] Karla, what took you so long?

449
00:17:54,531 --> 00:17:57,826
- [in English] Where have you been?
- Here, I bought banana cue.

450
00:17:57,910 --> 00:17:58,744
For all of us.

451
00:17:58,827 --> 00:18:00,204
- Oh, take some.
- Oh.

452
00:18:00,287 --> 00:18:01,789
[both, in English] Thank you.

453
00:18:01,872 --> 00:18:03,832
[Kurt] Okay, thank you.

454
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:05,042
One fell.

455
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:06,126
- [Kurt and Denden] Cheers.
- Oh.

456
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:08,128
[indistinct chattering]

457
00:18:08,212 --> 00:18:10,047
So, where's Uno?

458
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:12,800
I knew it. You like Uno too, huh?

459
00:18:12,883 --> 00:18:14,802
- You're just playing coy!
- Huh?

460
00:18:14,885 --> 00:18:17,137
- [giggles]
- [in English] Ah, Karla, just admit it.

461
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:19,181
[in English] All the girls here
have a crush on him.

462
00:18:19,264 --> 00:18:22,643
- And T-Bak said you do too.
- Really?

463
00:18:23,393 --> 00:18:25,729
Psst, that's just T-Bak.
Don't believe her!

464
00:18:26,438 --> 00:18:28,774
- [in English] Okay, okay, okay.
- Give me the banana cue!

465
00:18:29,358 --> 00:18:31,235
Actually, if you're looking for him,

466
00:18:31,318 --> 00:18:33,112
he went to Atoy's shop.

467
00:18:33,195 --> 00:18:36,657
Because Ame and Miss Cita are still there.

468
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:39,868
[ominous music playing]

469
00:18:43,831 --> 00:18:47,042
[tense music playing]

470
00:18:59,721 --> 00:19:01,640
[phone keypad beeping]

471
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:07,104
- [line ringing]
- [music intensifies]

472
00:19:07,938 --> 00:19:10,816
Sir, I found the room.

473
00:19:12,025 --> 00:19:13,318
But there's a problem.

474
00:19:15,237 --> 00:19:16,947
I don't know the access code.

475
00:19:17,531 --> 00:19:18,657
Do you know the combinations?

476
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:21,243
[music fades]

477
00:19:22,619 --> 00:19:23,787
All right.

478
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:25,330
Okay, I'll try it.

479
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:28,333
[tense music playing]

480
00:19:29,459 --> 00:19:34,173
[device blipping]

481
00:19:39,803 --> 00:19:41,180
[Ibyang] <i>Tatoy?</i>

482
00:19:42,347 --> 00:19:43,223
<i>Tatoy?</i>

483
00:19:43,807 --> 00:19:45,017
Yoo-hoo!

484
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:46,393
[pensive music playing]

485
00:19:46,476 --> 00:19:49,021
Ibyang? Ibyang?

486
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:51,440
Ibyang?

487
00:19:55,777 --> 00:19:57,029
Tatoy.

488
00:19:58,822 --> 00:20:00,324
I know

489
00:20:00,908 --> 00:20:03,327
that you're struggling,

490
00:20:03,410 --> 00:20:05,412
and surely you're hungry.

491
00:20:05,495 --> 00:20:08,081
[melancholic music playing]

492
00:20:08,165 --> 00:20:14,213
But don't ever think that you're alone.

493
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:19,009
[Atoy] <i>I could die here</i>
<i>and it would be over.</i>

494
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:23,305
Don't say that!

495
00:20:25,474 --> 00:20:31,104
Now is the time to apply
what you taught me before.

496
00:20:32,105 --> 00:20:36,485
And don't let negative thoughts
get all tangled up in your mind.

497
00:20:37,694 --> 00:20:40,656
Like thread

498
00:20:41,990 --> 00:20:43,408
through a needle.

499
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:47,871
It passes but doesn't stop.

500
00:20:50,123 --> 00:20:52,125
[Atoy] <i>I have no family.</i>

501
00:20:52,209 --> 00:20:54,461
<i>My life has no meaning anymore.</i>

502
00:20:55,504 --> 00:20:59,341
All the people who love you

503
00:20:59,424 --> 00:21:01,510
and care for you,

504
00:21:02,135 --> 00:21:04,263
they are your family!

505
00:21:07,641 --> 00:21:11,228
And I'm here too, Tatoy.

506
00:21:13,897 --> 00:21:16,400
You'll know me soon.

507
00:21:18,485 --> 00:21:22,072
So, don't give up, okay?

508
00:21:23,907 --> 00:21:25,742
[Atoy] <i>What are you saying?</i>

509
00:21:27,244 --> 00:21:31,415
Just have faith.

510
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:37,671
And don't lose hope.

511
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:40,382
Okay, Tatoy?

512
00:21:42,509 --> 00:21:43,969
Tatoy.

513
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,849
- Tatoy!
- [faded voice] <i>Atoy…</i>

514
00:21:50,017 --> 00:21:51,101
[Lily] Atoy.

515
00:21:51,184 --> 00:21:53,395
- [gasps]
- [music fades]

516
00:21:53,478 --> 00:21:54,730
[gasps softly]

517
00:21:54,813 --> 00:21:56,106
[Lily] Atoy.

518
00:21:57,024 --> 00:21:58,984
You must be dreaming.

519
00:21:59,526 --> 00:22:01,194
You were talking earlier.

520
00:22:02,195 --> 00:22:03,780
[gasping]

521
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:07,617
[somber music playing]

522
00:22:07,701 --> 00:22:09,119
It was Ibyang.

523
00:22:09,202 --> 00:22:10,412
[pants]

524
00:22:10,495 --> 00:22:12,247
I dreamt of Ibyang.

525
00:22:12,748 --> 00:22:14,374
She was talking to me.

526
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:18,003
You're right, Ibyang.

527
00:22:18,503 --> 00:22:21,381
I shouldn't think that no one…

528
00:22:21,465 --> 00:22:23,383
no one cares about me.

529
00:22:23,467 --> 00:22:26,928
- [panting]
- [melodramatic music playing]

530
00:22:27,012 --> 00:22:28,263
You're right.

531
00:22:29,431 --> 00:22:31,183
We need to escape from here.

532
00:22:33,977 --> 00:22:34,978
[groans]

533
00:22:35,604 --> 00:22:36,938
We need to get out.

534
00:22:37,022 --> 00:22:39,733
[groans]

535
00:22:39,816 --> 00:22:41,401
[Lily] I want that, but…

536
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:43,695
How will we do it?

537
00:22:43,779 --> 00:22:45,322
- [music fades]
- [Atoy panting]

538
00:22:45,906 --> 00:22:48,825
[rousing music playing]

539
00:22:58,794 --> 00:23:01,129
Boss, the police are outside.

540
00:23:01,213 --> 00:23:02,380
They're looking for you.

541
00:23:02,464 --> 00:23:04,508
[somber music playing]

542
00:23:06,093 --> 00:23:07,469
What did they say?

543
00:23:08,595 --> 00:23:09,971
Has someone reported us?

544
00:23:11,556 --> 00:23:12,849
No, boss.

545
00:23:14,684 --> 00:23:15,727
[in English] Good.

546
00:23:17,938 --> 00:23:20,982
Boss, what if Audrey
went to another police station?

547
00:23:21,066 --> 00:23:22,943
[ominous music playing]

548
00:23:23,026 --> 00:23:25,737
I already tipped off
the precincts we control.

549
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:29,825
If anyone reports there, I'll be informed.

550
00:23:34,746 --> 00:23:36,832
[Mongki] What about your dad, boss?

551
00:23:37,999 --> 00:23:39,292
[smirks]

552
00:23:42,671 --> 00:23:43,922
That's easy.

553
00:23:45,549 --> 00:23:47,717
I'll talk to the police myself.

554
00:23:51,304 --> 00:23:53,348
If Audrey didn't go there directly,

555
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:56,893
there's only one person they'll go to.

556
00:23:56,977 --> 00:23:58,228
[music fades]

557
00:23:58,311 --> 00:23:59,646
[Roger] Who, boss?

558
00:23:59,729 --> 00:24:03,066
[tense music playing]

559
00:24:19,624 --> 00:24:22,043
[footsteps approaching]

560
00:24:24,171 --> 00:24:26,506
[pensive music playing]

561
00:24:29,843 --> 00:24:32,804
[in English] Do you think
that we would not find out?

562
00:24:44,733 --> 00:24:48,028
[in English] Do you know this woman?

563
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:56,578
[in English] Don't tell me
that you don't know them.

564
00:25:08,340 --> 00:25:11,509
[suspicious music playing]

565
00:25:13,428 --> 00:25:15,931
[in English] You say you have no family.

566
00:25:16,765 --> 00:25:19,267
Don't drag them into this.

567
00:25:20,435 --> 00:25:22,354
[in English] You know I met this

568
00:25:24,064 --> 00:25:25,482
Audrey before?

569
00:25:26,650 --> 00:25:28,526
[Samir, in English] Hello, Ms. Audrey.

570
00:25:35,742 --> 00:25:38,662
[in English] She's a beautiful woman,
isn't she?

571
00:25:40,914 --> 00:25:44,542
[in English] I think even Mr. Dmitri
wanted her to be with me.

572
00:25:45,919 --> 00:25:48,588
[in English] That Audrey,

573
00:25:49,214 --> 00:25:53,260
she could have felt what a real man is.

574
00:25:55,011 --> 00:25:58,348
[in English] What a waste of a woman
now that she is with you.

575
00:26:02,269 --> 00:26:04,729
[in English] But I will still
make her scream.

576
00:26:04,813 --> 00:26:05,855
[music fades]

577
00:26:07,274 --> 00:26:09,234
[in English] Not in pleasure.

578
00:26:11,486 --> 00:26:13,446
[in English] But I will
make her scream in pain.

579
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:17,492
- [grunts]
- [music intensifies]

580
00:26:18,076 --> 00:26:20,036
If I find out you hurt them…

581
00:26:22,163 --> 00:26:24,374
I'll stitch you to the wall,

582
00:26:24,958 --> 00:26:28,044
feed you to animals like you.

583
00:26:29,129 --> 00:26:32,090
[in English] I don't even understand
your language, sir.

584
00:26:34,634 --> 00:26:35,844
[in English] Good luck with that.

585
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:12,255
- [electronic blipping]
- [tense music playing]

586
00:27:16,593 --> 00:27:19,429
That's Olga's child!
You're in trouble now.

587
00:27:19,512 --> 00:27:20,847
You're a fake daughter.

588
00:27:20,930 --> 00:27:22,682
Why do you say I'm fake?

589
00:27:22,766 --> 00:27:25,143
Olga's child is dead.

590
00:27:25,226 --> 00:27:27,562
[smirks] So, what are you?

591
00:27:27,645 --> 00:27:28,605
A ghost?

592
00:27:30,273 --> 00:27:32,275
- Are you with Ibyang?
- Olga ran away from me.

593
00:27:32,359 --> 00:27:34,444
This night has way too many screw-ups.

594
00:27:35,445 --> 00:27:36,529
[in English] We need that kid.

595
00:27:36,613 --> 00:27:37,906
We're safe here.

596
00:27:37,989 --> 00:27:41,242
How can we be safe, when Daddy isn't here?

597
00:27:41,326 --> 00:27:43,495
- [in English] I'm very, very hungry.
- [groans]

598
00:27:43,578 --> 00:27:45,538
[groaning]

599
00:27:45,622 --> 00:27:47,040
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

600
00:27:47,123 --> 00:27:48,625
UP NEXT

601
00:27:48,708 --> 00:27:49,584
[Atoy, in English] Cufflinks.

602
00:27:49,667 --> 00:27:52,712
We'll use these
in the first stage of our escape.

603
00:27:52,796 --> 00:27:55,173
- We're going to escape.
- ♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

604
00:27:55,256 --> 00:27:58,593
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

605
00:27:58,676 --> 00:28:00,261
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

606
00:28:00,345 --> 00:28:01,679
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
